From 94dc80c3383c3f75841b8d109ffa171800b74c75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 23:56:16 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] theme: add modal_surface_background so elevation has a
 fourth step

ElevationIndex::ElevatedSurface and ::ModalSurface both resolved to
elevated_surface_background, so the modal had no colour to step to and a
four-level ladder was unrepresentable. Adds modal_surface_background to
ThemeColors, exposes it as `modal_surface.background` in the theme JSON, and
points ModalSurface at it.

Every existing theme leaves the field unset, so it falls back to
elevated_surface_background at the refinement layer -- One, Ayu, Gruvbox and
every user theme render exactly as they do today. Without that fallback an unset
Hsla is transparent black, which would paint a black modal in every Zed theme;
the tests pin both halves and fail against the naive implementation.

This delivers the capability, not the step. The luminance ladder itself is theme
data and belongs to the Zeo palette.

Covers R2.1, R2.3.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
